1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,768
UGC clips need a quality bar: readable on mute, and a clear CTA.

2
00:00:04,768 --> 00:00:08,068
This lesson is about quality bar for ugc clips.

3
00:00:08,068 --> 00:00:09,902
Readable at mute; CTA clear.

4
00:00:09,902 --> 00:00:12,469
Do not treat this as theory only.

5
00:00:12,469 --> 00:00:16,136
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

6
00:00:16,136 --> 00:00:21,637
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

7
00:00:21,637 --> 00:00:25,671
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

8
00:00:25,671 --> 00:00:30,072
Stay practical: define your quality bar before you optimize branding or tools.

9
00:00:30,392 --> 00:00:36,949
Define your bar: text on screen, one idea, face or demo visible, CTA in the last seconds.

10
00:00:36,949 --> 00:00:39,649
Remember the objective: define your quality bar.

11
00:00:39,649 --> 00:00:43,892
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

12
00:00:43,892 --> 00:00:48,521
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

13
00:00:48,521 --> 00:00:52,763
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

14
00:00:52,763 --> 00:00:57,392
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

15
00:00:57,712 --> 00:01:01,231
If it fails on mute, it fails in the feed.

16
